    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44261" root="&#xA;                        هدى&#xA;                    " body-key="h1">
                        
                            1
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَدَاهُ</span></b> 
                        
                        <i>He directed him,</i> or <i>guided him,</i> to the
way; (K, * TA;) <i>directed him aright;</i> or <i>caused
him to take,</i> or <i>follow, a right way</i> or <i>course</i> or
<i>direction.</i> (K, TA.) See 8. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَدَى العَرُوسَ</span>
                        <i>He sent</i> [or <i>conducted</i>] <i>the bride</i> (MA, KL) to
her husband, (MA,) or to the house of her husband: (KL;) <i>i. q.</i>
                        <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَفَّهَا</span>, (K in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زف</span>,) and so
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَهْدَاهَا</span></b> . (Msb in that art.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَهْدِى</span> meaning
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يُؤَدِّى</span>: see an ex. in a verse cited voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَبَعٌ</span>.

